  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique Human Development Integrated Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">?Improve education outcomes of school-aged children in the most vulnerable districts of Mozambique by using schools as platforms for integrated service delivery.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation aims to improve human development outcomes in Mozambique through integrated service delivery and climate-resilient infrastructure. It comprises four components: (1) An integrated package of HD services focusing on teacher training, social support for students, and school-based health services; (2) Climate-resilient and energy-efficient school infrastructure improvements to modernize basic schools and establish digital learning hubs; (3) Institutional strengthening to enhance service maintenance through improved school management and local capacity building; and (4) A Contingent Emergency Response Component for immediate crisis response. The project emphasizes cross-ministerial coordination, digital solutions, and climate resilience while incorporating Performance-Based Conditions to ensure effective implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
